{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureStability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureStability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinedParticle","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ElectronShell","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DressedParticle","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.ConfinementSDP"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureStability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureStability","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L182-L192","doc":"**Shell-closure stability (headline).** Umbrella statement:\nfor a noble-gas-dressed particle, binding multiplicity ≥ 2 and\nany subsequent one-step dressing cannot reduce Frobenius\nstability. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:shell-closure-stability","label":"prop:shell-closure-stability","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/shell-closure-stability.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.shell_closure_terminality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.shell_closure_terminality","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L159-L178","doc":"**Shell-closure stability, claim (3) — terminality.**\nFor `Z ∈ nobleGasMagic`, any outgoing dressing from `D` to a\n`D'` with `Z + 1` electrons requires simultaneously breaking\n`μ ≥ 2` tight dual blocks of the confinement SDP.\nStated here as: the stability of any strict upgrade does not\nexceed that of `D` in the generic locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.shell_closure_noble_multiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.shell_closure_noble_multiplicity","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L146-L155","doc":"**Shell-closure stability, claim (2) — noble-gas multiplicity.**\nAt `Z ∈ nobleGasMagic`, the binding multiplicity satisfies\n`μ(S, q) ≥ 2`, giving the multi-operator regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.shell_closure_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.shell_closure_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L130-L142","doc":"**Shell-closure stability, claim (1) — monotone non-decrease.**\nPer-instance form backed by `ShellClosureMonotone`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.shellClosureMonotone_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.shellClosureMonotone_refl","kind":"instance","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L117-L128","doc":"**Reflexivity instance**: when `D_prev = D` syntactically, the\nmonotonicity is `≤` reflexivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureMonotone.monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureMonotone.monotone","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Stability index does not decrease under the one-step dressing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureMonotone.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureMonotone.mk","kind":"ctor","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureMonotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ShellClosureMonotone","kind":"class","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L97-L115","doc":"**Shell-closure monotonicity — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\n\nWitnesses non-decrease of the Frobenius stability index for a\n*specific* one-step dressing pair. The full SDP-relaxation\nmonotonicity proof requires the cabling embedding\n`ι : H_{A+Z-1}(q) ↪ H_{A+Z}(q)` and the dual-feasible lift,\nwhich depend on Mathlib SDP infrastructure. By packaging the\ninequality as a class, the conjectural content is visible at\nevery use site rather than asserted universally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.isOneStepDressing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.isOneStepDressing","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L89-L93","doc":"Is `D` a one-step dressing of `D_prev` (one extra electron)? ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusStability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frobeniusStability","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L84-L87","doc":"Frobenius stability accessor, backed by `HasFrobeniusStability`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasFrobeniusStability.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasFrobeniusStability.sigma","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The stability index `σ_F(D, q)`, real-valued: it is an SDP dual\nobjective, and it is compared with `≤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasFrobeniusStability.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasFrobeniusStability.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HasFrobeniusStability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HasFrobeniusStability","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ShellClosureStability.lean#L47-L82","doc":"Frobenius stability data — class-supplied evaluation of\n`σ_F(D, q) = n_target · y₀*(D, q)` (the optimal dual objective\nof the confinement SDP at `(D, q)`; equivalently, by strong\nduality, the optimal primal `⟨T, Φ*⟩`).\n\n**The index is `ℝ`-valued, and that is the whole point (2026-09-02).**\nIt used to be `R_q → R_q`, and because `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` carries no\norder, this file installed one:\n\n    local instance : LE R_q := ⟨fun _ _ => True⟩\n\nUnder that instance `x ≤ y` is `True` for every pair, so claim (1) below\n— *\"the stability index is non-decreasing along the dressing chain\"* —\nwas `True`, and `ShellClosureMonotone` was inhabited by `⟨trivial⟩` for\n**any** pair of dressed particles, one-step or not. Measured\n`lean`-direct, exit 0, with the instance in scope:\n\n    example (x y : R_q) : x ≤ y := trivial\n    example … : frobeniusStability D_prev q ≤ frobeniusStability D q := trivial\n    example … : ShellClosureMonotone D_prev D q h := ⟨trivial⟩\n\nAn ordering is an archimedean construct (AGENTS.md §7c), so it belongs\non the `ℝ` side of the substrate wall, not on the Laurent ring. `σ_F` is\nan SDP dual objective and is a real number; making that explicit removes\nthe need for a fabricated order and makes claim (1) falsifiable. The\nargument stays `R_q` — the *point* of evaluation is still substrate-side.\n\n**Claim (2) was never affected**, and this is worth separating rather\nthan sweeping in: `bindingMultiplicity` is `ℕ`-valued, so `μ ≥ 2` is over\n`ℕ`'s genuine order. The same probe rejects `… ≥ 2 := trivial` with a\ntype mismatch. Only the `σ_F` comparisons collapsed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}